????
### What is Circular Dependency?

**Interview answer:**

> **Circular dependency occurs when two or more objects depend on each other directly or indirectly. In other words, Object A depends on Object B, and Object B depends on Object A, creating a circular dependency.**

### Simple example

```text
Class A → depends on Class B
Class B → depends on Class A
```

So:

```text
A → B → A → B → ...
```

### Spring Boot example

```java
class UserService {
    private OrderService orderService;
}

class OrderService {
    private UserService userService;
}
```

Here:

```text
UserService → OrderService
OrderService → UserService
```

This is a **circular dependency**.

### How to solve it?

> **We can solve circular dependency by redesigning the classes, removing unnecessary dependencies, introducing a third service, or using dependency inversion. In Spring, constructor injection is preferred because it helps identify circular dependencies early.**

### ⭐ Short interview answer

> **“Circular dependency occurs when two or more classes depend on each other directly or indirectly. We can resolve it by redesigning the dependencies and following proper separation of responsibilities.”**
