Agar interviewer poochhe **“What is dependency and how do you support/manage it in Spring Boot?”**, to ye proper answer do:

### 1. What is Dependency?

> **A dependency means that one class or component requires another class or component to perform its work. In simple words, when one object depends on another object, it is called a dependency.**

### Example

```java
class OrderService {
    private PaymentService paymentService;
}
```

Here, `OrderService` depends on `PaymentService`.

```text
OrderService → PaymentService
```

### 2. How does Spring Boot support dependency?

> **Spring Boot supports dependency management and Dependency Injection through the Spring IoC container. Spring creates and manages the required objects and injects them into the dependent class.**

Example:

```java
@Service
public class PaymentService {
}
```

```java
@Service
public class OrderService {

    private final PaymentService paymentService;

    public OrderService(PaymentService paymentService) {
        this.paymentService = paymentService;
    }
}
```

Here Spring automatically provides `PaymentService` to `OrderService`.

This is called **Dependency Injection (DI)**.

### ⭐ Interview-ready full answer

> **“Dependency means when one class requires another class to perform its functionality. Spring Boot supports dependency management using the IoC container and Dependency Injection. The Spring container creates and manages objects and injects the required dependencies into the dependent classes. Constructor injection is generally preferred because it makes dependencies explicit and improves testability.”**
